# Prettier has no parser for these files, so `prettier --check .` must skip
# them rather than fail. Both are Git plumbing/config, not source.
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Build output and dependencies.
dist/
build/
coverage/
node_modules/

# Generated release and coverage artifacts.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated benchmark report. `tests/unit/analysis/consistency/benchmark/
# report.test.ts` compares this file byte-for-byte against a fresh render, so
# Prettier must not reformat its markdown tables. Regenerate it with
# `WRITE_BENCHMARK=1 npx vitest run .../benchmark/report.test.ts`.
docs/consistency-benchmark.md

# External specification documents, not repository source.
#
# `systematic review/` holds the incoming product specifications the
# implementation plans are written against. They are inputs, not code: they
# are authored outside the repository's Prettier settings, they are not linted,
# and reformatting them would produce a large diff against a document whose
# exact wording is the thing under review. Formatting them is a no-op for the
# build and a real edit to someone else's prose, so they are excluded rather
# than silently rewritten. Remove this entry once the folder is either
# formatted deliberately or moved outside the repository.
systematic review/
